#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/10
msgid ""
"From the first time we met.\n"
msgstr ""
"初见就看穿了。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/11
msgid ""
"I wish you'd told me...\n"
msgstr ""
"真希望你告诉过我……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/12
msgid ""
"Sorry. I didn't know if it'd be right.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。我不确定该不该说。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/13
msgid ""
"You might have gotten mixed up in things you\n"
"shouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能卷入了你\n"
"不该卷入的事情。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/14
msgid ""
"That is impressive, though. Sizing him up him at a\n"
"single glance.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过那真厉害。一眼就\n"
"看穿了他。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/15
msgid ""
"He reeked.\n"
msgstr ""
"他一身味儿。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/16
msgid ""
"Reeked?\n"
msgstr ""
"味？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/17
msgid ""
"He had this unmistakable air about him...\n"
msgstr ""
"他身上有股藏不住的气息……\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/18
msgid ""
"The air of someone who's been given a mission\n"
"and will see it through no matter what.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种被赋予使命、无论如何都要\n"
"完成的人的气质。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/19
msgid ""
"Like me. I could just smell it.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟我一样。一闻就知。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/20
msgid ""
"That is amazing, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"太厉害了，SNAKE！\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/21
msgid ""
"Nah, I'm just kidding. It was his prosthetic hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪有，开玩笑的。是他的假手。\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/22
msgid ""
"Why would a professor from a peace university\n"
"need a tool for assassination?\n"
msgstr ""
"和平大学的教授\n"
"要暗杀工具做什么？\n"

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/23
msgid ""
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 473..1365
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/0
msgid ""
"Are there any large-scale ruins in Costa Rica, Paz?\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加有大型遗迹吗，帕兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2410
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/1
msgid ""
"There's a place east of Cartago called Guayabo.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡塔戈东边有个地方叫瓜亚沃。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 2493..3232
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/2
msgid ""
"They have ruins there, but they're not especially\n"
"big.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里有遗迹，但不算\n"
"特别大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 3650..4486
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/3
msgid ""
"Not the place I'm thinking of... Any others?\n"
msgstr ""
"不是我想的地方……还有别的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 4527..5935
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, if you go a little way across the border into\n"
"Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，越过边境进入\n"
"尼加拉瓜不远，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 6004..8219
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/5
msgid ""
"there's a place called La Fortaleza de la\n"
"Inmaculada Concepción. That's the only famous one.\n"
msgstr ""
"有个地方叫拉福塔莱萨·德·拉\n"
"因玛库拉达·康塞普西翁。就它出名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 8261..9195
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/6
msgid ""
"Then what were those ruins I saw from up on\n"
"Irazu...?\n"
msgstr ""
"那我在伊拉苏山上\n"
"看到的遗迹是……？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 9250..10783
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/7
msgid ""
"There are a lot of things we still do not know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations.\n"
msgstr ""
"关于哥斯达黎加的古代文明，\n"
"我们还有很多未知。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 10839..11730
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/8
msgid ""
"There are giant stone spheres throughout the\n"
"country.\n"
msgstr ""
"全国各地都有巨大的\n"
"石球。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 11814..12719
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/9
msgid ""
"What they were used for is still a mystery.\n"
msgstr ""
"用途至今是个谜。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/0
msgid ""
"Paz, you said Costa Rica has no army, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹，你说过哥斯达黎加没有军队吧？\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/1
msgid ""
"Correct. Article 12 of the constitution declared\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。宪法第12条宣布\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/2
msgid ""
"that the army as a permanent institution is\n"
"abolished.\n"
msgstr ""
"军队作为一个常设机构\n"
"被废除。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/3
msgid ""
"It does permit us to organize armed forces for\n"
"national defense\n"
msgstr ""
"它确实允许我们组织武装力量用于\n"
"国防\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/4
msgid ""
"based on inter-American treaties.\n"
msgstr ""
"按美洲国家条约组建。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/5
msgid ""
"Only temporarily, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"那只是暂时的。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/6
msgid ""
"In effect, yes. But in the years since the\n"
"constitution took effect,\n"
msgstr ""
"实际上，是的。但自\n"
"宪法生效以来的这些年里，\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/7
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has not once raised an army.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加从未组建军队。\n"

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/0
msgid ""
"Paz. How does your country defend itself without\n"
"an army?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/1
msgid ""
"Especially in a rough neighborhood like Central\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/2
msgid ""
"With the right kind of diplomacy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/3
msgid ""
"If we live up to our ideals and earn the respect of\n"
"other countries,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/4
msgid ""
"the international community will support us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/5
msgid ""
"The two times Nicaragua actually did invade,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/6
msgid ""
"the conflict was resolved diplomatically under OAS\n"
"(Organization of American States) auspices.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/7
msgid ""
"Doesn't that leave you depending on the U.S. after\n"
"all?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/8
msgid ""
"American influence is unmatched, it is true.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/9
msgid ""
"San Jose was critical of American policy at the\n"
"time...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/10
msgid ""
"But America supported us all the same. It was\n"
"because we practiced peaceful diplomacy...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/11
msgid ""
"That is what I like to think.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/12
msgid ""
"That's one way to approach it, sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/13
msgid ""
"But there are countries out there who'll use force\n"
"no matter how bad it looks.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/14
msgid ""
"Maybe so... I know my way of thinking probably\n"
"looks naïve to you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/15
msgid ""
"But it's not like we expect peace without working\n"
"for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/16
msgid ""
"Diplomacy is a battle in itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb5b70/17
msgid ""
"And we have to make the effort\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 473..1783
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/0
msgid ""
"The army was abolished 25 years ago, the year\n"
"after the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"军队在25年前被废除，也就是\n"
"内战后的第二年。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2869
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/1
msgid ""
"I learned about the sorrow of civil war from a very\n"
"young age.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从很小的时候\n"
"就了解到内战的悲伤。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2995..4165
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/2
msgid ""
"The futility of countrymen fighting each other, and\n"
"the tragedy...\n"
msgstr ""
"同胞互相残杀的徒劳，以及\n"
"那场悲剧……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5377
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/3
msgid ""
"Costa Rica learned the hard way. That is why it\n"
"abolished its army.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加吃了大亏。所以才\n"
"废除了军队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6394
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/4
msgid ""
"It decided to pour its efforts into education\n"
"instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"它决定转而将努力投入到\n"
"教育中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 6548..7272
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/5
msgid ""
"\"More teachers than soldiers\" was the slogan.\n"
msgstr ""
"口号是“教师多于士兵”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8080
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/6
msgid ""
"Education is essential, no question.\n"
msgstr ""
"教育必不可少。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8247..9334
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/7
msgid ""
"Even Che used to teach reading and writing in\n"
"between guerrilla campaigns.\n"
msgstr ""
"就连切·格瓦拉也曾在\n"
"游击战间隙教人读书写字。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10644
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/8
msgid ""
"Costa Rica was poor at the time. We didn't have\n"
"many resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时哥斯达黎加很穷。我们\n"
"没有多少资源。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10811..12246
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/9
msgid ""
"I suppose we had to pick one or the other - the\n"
"military or the schools.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想我们只能二选一——要么\n"
"军队，要么学校。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/0
msgid ""
"Kaz was telling me Japan has a peace constitution,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹告诉我，日本也有\n"
"一部和平宪法。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/1
msgid ""
"That is right. Apparently when Costa Rica was\n"
"drafting its constitution,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。据说哥斯达黎加在\n"
"起草宪法时，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/2
msgid ""
"they looked to the Japanese as a model.\n"
msgstr ""
"就以日本为范本。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/3
msgid ""
"Only Japan's constitution renounces war itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"只是日本宪法连战争权都放弃了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/5
msgid ""
"But... Japan has a Self-Defense Force, right? That I\n"
"do not get.\n"
msgstr ""
"但……日本有自卫队，对吧？这我\n"
"就不懂了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/6
msgid ""
"I think I will ask Mr. Miller about it next time I see\n"
"him. He said he used to be in the JSDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想下次见到米勒先生时问问他。\n"
"他说他以前在自卫队待过。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/7
msgid ""
"You're a curious one, aren't you? Don't study too\n"
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""
"你真好奇。别太\n"
"用功了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/0
msgid ""
"What was that you were saying... \"peace is not the\n"
"natural state of men\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你刚才说什么来着……“和平并非\n"
"人类的天性”？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/1
msgid ""
"You said you learned it in school.\n"
msgstr ""
"你说这是在学校学的。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/2
msgid ""
"That's right. They're the words of the German\n"
"philosopher Immanuel Kant.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。这是德国\n"
"哲学家伊曼努尔·康德的话。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/3
msgid ""
"In 1795 he wrote a book titled \"Perpetual Peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"1795年他写了本书叫《永久和平》。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/4
msgid ""
"Kant argued that it's precisely because peace is\n"
"unnatural\n"
msgstr ""
"康德认为，正因为和平是\n"
"非自然的，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/5
msgid ""
"that we have to make it ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"才要靠我们自己去创造。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/6
msgid ""
"How?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么创造？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/7
msgid ""
"That's what his book is about. Is the concept\n"
"starting to sound interesting now?\n"
msgstr ""
"他书里就讲这个。现在这理念\n"
"听着有意思了？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/8
msgid ""
"Not really... I belong in a more natural world.\n"
msgstr ""
"还好……我更适合自然的世界。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/9
msgid ""
"Is that so...\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗……\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/10
msgid ""
"...My grandparents died in the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我祖父母死于内战。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/11
msgid ""
"If only we'd been at peace, they wouldn't have lost\n"
"their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"要是我们身处和平，他们就不会\n"
"丧命了。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/12
msgid ""
"You actually wish for war?\n"
msgstr ""
"你其实渴望战争？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/13
msgid ""
"It's not like I want to hurt innocent civilians.\n"
msgstr ""
"我又不是想伤害无辜平民。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/14
msgid ""
"But if someone attacks you, what are you\n"
"supposed to do?\n"
msgstr ""
"但如果有人攻击你，你\n"
"该怎么办？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/15
msgid ""
"A country needs the strength to defend itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家必须有自卫的力量。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/16
msgid ""
"Otherwise it faces invasion, oppression, political\n"
"subjugation.\n"
msgstr ""
"否则它就会面临侵略、压迫、政治\n"
"征服。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/17
msgid ""
"If they'd simply stop using force to tangle with\n"
"each other,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果他们干脆停止使用武力来互相\n"
"纠缠，\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/18
msgid ""
"countries wouldn't need force to defend themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家就不需要武力自卫。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/19
msgid ""
"And how would you guarantee that?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你怎么保证？\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/20
msgid ""
"I...\n"
msgstr ""
"我……\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/21
msgid ""
"...Sorry. But you have to understand how the world\n"
"works\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉。但你得明白世界\n"
"怎么运转\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/22
msgid ""
"in order to protect the ones you love.\n"
msgstr ""
"才能保护你所爱的人。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/23
msgid ""
"That's not to say ideals aren't important, too. They\n"
"are.\n"
msgstr ""
"这并不是说理想就不重要。它们\n"
"很重要。\n"

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/24
msgid ""
"You are right, Snake... Thanks. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"你说得对，SNAKE……谢谢。和平！\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica's forests are more diverse than you\n"
"might expect.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的森林比你\n"
"想象的更加多样。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/1
msgid ""
"Not all of them are tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"不全是热带雨林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/2
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is close to the Equator, it is true, but it\n"
"is also very mountainous.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加确实靠近赤道，但它\n"
"也非常多山。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/3
msgid ""
"I see what you mean.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂你意思。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/4
msgid ""
"Go up 4,000 feet in elevation and the temperature\n"
"drops more than seven degrees.\n"
msgstr ""
"海拔每升高4000英尺，气温\n"
"就会下降超过七度。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/5
msgid ""
"There are basically three types of forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"森林基本分三类。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/6
msgid ""
"The lowlands are covered in tropical rain forests,\n"
"the highlands by tropical cloud forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"低地覆盖着热带雨林，\n"
"高地则覆盖着热带云雾林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/7
msgid ""
"And areas where there is a dry season have\n"
"tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"而有旱季的地区则分布着\n"
"热带干燥森林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 473..2034
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/0
msgid ""
"The lowlands along the Caribbean coast are mostly\n"
"covered by hot, humid tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"加勒比海岸沿线的低地大部分\n"
"覆盖着炎热潮湿的热带雨林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 2131..2897
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/1
msgid ""
"What most people envision when they think of\n"
"\"jungle.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"多数人想到\n"
"“丛林”时的画面。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 3009..4374
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/2
msgid ""
"The closely packed trees spread their branches\n"
"out at great heights to soak up the sun.\n"
msgstr ""
"茂密拥挤的树木在高处\n"
"伸展枝叶，以吸收阳光。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/3
msgid ""
"Their shade makes it dark near the ground, so be\n"
"careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"树荫让地面附近很暗，要\n"
"小心。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 5600..6757
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/4
msgid ""
"Of course, with so little light few plants can grow\n"
"on the ground,\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，光太少，没几株植物能长在\n"
"地上，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 6812..7439
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/5
msgid ""
"so it might actually be easier to walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"那走路可能反而更轻松。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 7481..8791
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/6
msgid ""
"So even if you could photosynthesize, it wouldn't\n"
"do you any good.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以就算你能光合作用，也没\n"
"好处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 8860..9738
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/7
msgid ""
"Photosynthesize? People cannot do that.\n"
msgstr ""
"光合作用？人做不到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 10128..10602
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/8
msgid ""
"Most people, anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"多数人不行。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/0
msgid ""
"Areas with a distinct dry season, like the Pacific\n"
"coast, have tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""
"有明显旱季的地区，比如太平洋沿岸，\n"
"分布着热带干林。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/1
msgid ""
"During the dry season, the trees drop their leaves.\n"
"It gives you a clearer view,\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季时，树木会落叶。\n"
"这让你视野更清晰，\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/2
msgid ""
"but at the same time there are fewer places to\n"
"hide, so be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"但同时也少了可以\n"
"躲藏的地方，所以要小心。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/3
msgid ""
"Sounds dull.\n"
msgstr ""
"听着挺无聊。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/4
msgid ""
"It is not, really. A lot of trees flower during the dry\n"
"season.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实并不是。很多树在旱季\n"
"开花。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/5
msgid ""
"Including my favorite, the tabebuia.\n"
msgstr ""
"包括我最喜欢的黄花风铃木。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/6
msgid ""
"It has these amazingly vivid yellow flowers.\n"
msgstr ""
"开着极其鲜艳的黄花。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/0
msgid ""
"The cloud forests cover the central mountainous\n"
"region of the country.\n"
msgstr ""
"云雾林覆盖着该国的中部\n"
"山区。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/1
msgid ""
"They're perpetually shrouded in fog. You get wet\n"
"just standing there.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们常年笼罩在雾中。你光是\n"
"站在那里就会湿透。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/2
msgid ""
"It is as if the entire forest is inside a cloud.\n"
msgstr ""
"仿佛整片森林都在云里。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/3
msgid ""
"Must make for poor visibility.\n"
msgstr ""
"那视野肯定很差。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/4
msgid ""
"It does. But beauty, too. It is like being lost in some\n"
"mystical, green labyrinth.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实。但也美。像迷失在某个\n"
"神秘绿色迷宫。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/5
msgid ""
"...I'd rather not get lost if that's OK.\n"
msgstr ""
"……可以的话，我不想迷路。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/6
msgid ""
"The forests are also home to lots of rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""
"森林里还栖息着许多珍稀动物。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/7
msgid ""
"Especially brightly colored frogs. They like the\n"
"humidity.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是色彩鲜艳的青蛙。它们喜欢\n"
"潮湿。\n"

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/0
msgid ""
"You know that butterfly painted on Peace Walker -\n"
"any idea what that is?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/1
msgid ""
"...It is a Morpho. A Peleides Morpho, if I'm not\n"
"mistaken.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/2
msgid ""
"Peleides Morpho?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/3
msgid ""
"Uh huh. It is the most common type of Morpho in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5739..5935
#: codec/1/183/0xb7ea0/4
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/4
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/6
msgid ""
"Huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is said to have about 87,000 species\n"
"of living things.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说哥斯达黎加约有87,000种\n"
"生物。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2925
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/1
#, c-format
msgid ""
"That's about 5% of all the known species in the\n"
"world.\n"
msgstr ""
"这大约占世界上所有已知物种的\n"
"5%。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4235
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/2
msgid ""
"A tiny place like this? I'll be damned.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么小的地方？真没想到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4263..5057
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/3
msgid ""
"I want to protect that biological diversity.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想保护这种生物多样性。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6102
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/4
msgid ""
"When diversity is lost, the environment weakens.\n"
msgstr ""
"多样性一失，环境就弱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6185..6729
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/5
msgid ""
"Just look at the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"看看种植园吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6784..8192
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/6
msgid ""
"I think I know what you mean. It's like trying to\n"
"assemble a unit from similar guys\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂你的意思。就像用一群相似的人\n"
"组队\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8331..8958
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/7
msgid ""
"- it usually doesn't work out.\n"
msgstr ""
"往往行不通。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8986..10017
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/8
msgid ""
"Throw a few square pegs in there and everything\n"
"falls into place.\n"
msgstr ""
"掺几个格格不入的人进去，一切\n"
"就顺了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 10058..11243
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/9
msgid ""
"There are so many species here that a lot of them\n"
"have not even been classified yet.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里物种太多了，很多\n"
"连分类都还没做。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 11312..12678
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/10
msgid ""
"I'm hoping I can help do that someday. Kind of like\n"
"a parataxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""
"希望有朝一日我也能帮上忙。有点像\n"
"副分类学家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 12692..13527
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/11
msgid ""
"Para... say that again?\n"
msgstr ""
"副……再说？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14503
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/12
msgid ""
"Parataxonomist. Someone who helps a taxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""
"副分类学家。协助分类学家的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16147
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/13
msgid ""
"Oh. Huh. I thought you were going to say it had\n"
"something to do with parachutes.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。哈。我还以为你要说\n"
"跟降落伞有关。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 16551..16913
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/14
msgid ""
"You're weird...\n"
msgstr ""
"你真怪……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 473..2131
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/0
msgid ""
"The Development Corporation of Costa Rica, or\n"
"CODESA, was established two years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加开发公司，简称\n"
"CODESA，两年前成立。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3023
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/1
msgid ""
"Since President Oduber was elected this year,\n"
msgstr ""
"今年奥杜贝尔总统当选后，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3914
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/2
msgid ""
"the state has been putting a lot more effort into\n"
"development.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家在开发上投入了更多\n"
"精力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4736
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/3
msgid ""
"The corporate state, so to speak.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以说是公司化国家。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4778..5767
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/4
msgid ""
"Growth is good and all, but there's one thing that\n"
"bugs me.\n"
msgstr ""
"发展是好事，但有件事让我\n"
"在意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..5976
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/5
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/37
msgid ""
"What's that?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么事？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6004..7258
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/6
msgid ""
"I cannot help but wonder whether CODESA is not\n"
"just a front for la CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不禁怀疑CODESA是不是\n"
"CIA的幌子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7286..7843
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/7
msgid ""
"You mean what the \"professor\" was saying\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说那位“教授”说的\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7843..8721
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/8
msgid ""
"about the CIA mercenaries posing as security\n"
"guards?\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA雇佣兵冒充保安\n"
"的事？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8763..9404
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/9
msgid ""
"They were using CODESA as camouflage...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们拿CODESA当掩护……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10295
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/10
msgid ""
"I'm worried that development is going to destroy\n"
"the forests...\n"
msgstr ""
"我担心开发会毁掉\n"
"森林……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 10435..11257
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/11
msgid ""
"but I do not suppose it has anything to do with this.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我想这跟那事无关。\n"

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/0
msgid ""
"My mother was the one who named me \"Paz.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/1
msgid ""
"She said it was an expression of her wish that the\n"
"country stay at peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/184/0xb8ee0/2
msgid ""
"It's a pretty common name in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 473..975
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/0
msgid ""
"You like the peace sign, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"你喜欢和平手势啊？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1003..2340
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/1
msgid ""
"Sí. As a gesture it connects every peace-loving\n"
"person.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。这个手势连接着每个\n"
"爱好和平的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3441
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/2
msgid ""
"Here, you try it, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"来，你试试，SNAKE。和平！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4388
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/3
msgid ""
"...No thanks. It... doesn't suit me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不了。那……不适合我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4444..4862
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/4
msgid ""
"Too bad for you.\n"
msgstr ""
"算你倒霉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6032
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/5
msgid ""
"You know, the \"V\" in the peace sign comes from\n"
"the \"V\" in \"Victory.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"和平手势的\"V\"来自\n"
"\"Victory\"（胜利）的\"V\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6199..6882
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/6
msgid ""
"When did it start standing for peace?\n"
msgstr ""
"它何时开始代表和平？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6952..7648
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/7
msgid ""
"I am not completely sure... but\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不太确定……不过\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 7774..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/8
msgid ""
"I guess it came out of the protest movement\n"
"against the Vietnam War.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想是出自反越南战争的\n"
"抗议运动吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/9
msgid ""
"Oh, and don't turn your hand around when you do\n"
"it,\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，还有，做的时候别把手转过来\n"
"，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10699
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/10
msgid ""
"especially around British people. It is insulting.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其在英国人面前。那是侮辱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 487..1072
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/0
msgid ""
"So you live alone now?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你现在一个人住？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1086..2605
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/1
msgid ""
"No, not alone. I've been living in school dormitories\n"
"since I started junior high.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不是一个人。我上初中起\n"
"就一直住学校宿舍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2688..4304
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/2
msgid ""
"After my mother died, my relatives took me in,\n"
"but... they were not my real family.\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲去世后，亲戚收留了我，\n"
"但……他们不是我的家人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4332..4709
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/3
msgid ""
"You didn't fit in there?\n"
msgstr ""
"你融不进去？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4722..5544
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/4
msgid ""
"In a way... My aunts were kind to me and all...\n"
msgstr ""
"某种程度……姨妈们对我也好……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5698..7077
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/5
msgid ""
"But I know how difficult it must have been to\n"
"suddenly have a child thrust into their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我知道，突然有个孩子闯进\n"
"她们的生活有多难。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7927
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/6
msgid ""
"When you live with someone, there are no secrets.\n"
msgstr ""
"和人一起生活，是藏不住秘密的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8108..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/7
msgid ""
"I could tell my being there was a burden on them...\n"
msgstr ""
"我看得出我的存在是他们的负担……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9209..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/8
msgid ""
"Sounds like a rough childhood.\n"
msgstr ""
"你童年听着挺苦。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10922
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/9
msgid ""
"I would not say that. I was lucky just to have\n"
"people to take me in.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不这么觉得。有人肯收留我\n"
"已经很幸运了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10964..12162
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/10
msgid ""
"There are huérfanos living out in the streets\n"
"because their mothers died.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有孤儿因为母亲死了\n"
"流落街头。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12246..13165
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/11
msgid ""
"It is even worse in countries with frequent civil\n"
"wars.\n"
msgstr ""
"在战乱频发的国家\n"
"更惨。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 13221..14113
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/12
msgid ""
"So who am I to complain about my childhood?\n"
msgstr ""
"我哪有资格抱怨自己的童年？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14154..14628
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/13
msgid ""
"You're a pretty tough kid, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你这孩子挺坚强的嘛。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14656..15562
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/14
msgid ""
"...Not at all. I am not strong at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"……才没。我一点不坚强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 473..1003
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/0
msgid ""
"I have a favor to ask you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，我想求你件事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1044..1226
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/1
msgid ""
"Name it.\n"
msgstr ""
"说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2215
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/2
msgid ""
"I want to you to give me a job here. I want to help\n"
"out.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想让你在这给我个工作。我想帮\n"
"忙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 2243..3148
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/3
msgid ""
"You sure? You just went through a hell of a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"你确定？你刚经历了一场大难。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 3287..3970
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/4
msgid ""
"You should probably take it easy until you're\n"
"settled.\n"
msgstr ""
"你最好先放松，等安顿下来\n"
"再说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4904
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/5
msgid ""
"Thank you. But there must be something I can do.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。但我总得做点什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6116
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/6
msgid ""
"You would not want me near a gun, but I am a\n"
"decent cook.\n"
msgstr ""
"你别让我碰枪，不过我做菜还\n"
"不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6826
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/7
msgid ""
"Now there's a skill we can use.\n"
msgstr ""
"这本事正好用得上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6854..7885
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/8
msgid ""
"Put me on the mess hall team - I think I can handle\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"把我排到食堂组，我觉得我能\n"
"应付。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 8010..9250
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/9
msgid ""
"Once I get used to it, I'll even add in some Costa\n"
"Rican recipes.\n"
msgstr ""
"等我习惯了，我还会加一些哥斯达黎加\n"
"菜谱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9780
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/10
msgid ""
"Sounds like a plan.\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么定了。\n"

#: codec/1/185/0xb9ef0/0
msgid ""
"Playa del Alba means \"beach of dawn.\" The morning\n"
"sun is so beautiful over the Caribbean.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/185/0xb9ef0/1
msgid ""
"Beach of Dawn, huh? Perfect place to start a\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/185/0xb9ef0/4
msgid "7"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/185/0xb9ef0/7
msgid "AQ"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/0
msgid ""
"Bosque del Alba means \"forest of dawn.\" Naturally,\n"
"it is situated on the east coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bosque del Alba 的意思是“黎明之林”。自然，\n"
"它位于东海岸。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/1
msgid ""
"It is your standard tropical rainforest, everything\n"
"you'd imagine in a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是标准的热带雨林，你能想象到的\n"
"丛林里的一切。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/2
msgid ""
"No sign of morning sun here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里见不到晨光。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/3
msgid ""
"The foliage is too thick for direct sunlight to hit\n"
"the floor.\n"
msgstr ""
"枝叶太茂密，阳光无法直接照到\n"
"地面。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/4
msgid ""
"I do not know how easy it will be making your way\n"
"through here.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道你在这里穿行会有多\n"
"容易。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/5
msgid ""
"I'll be fine. This isn't my first trip to a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没事。这又不是我第一次进丛林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 473..1727
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/0
msgid ""
"The mercenaries' supply base is situated on\n"
"elevated ground by the coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"雇佣兵的补给基地坐落在海岸边的\n"
"高地上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 1825..2981
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/1
msgid ""
"I heard them call it \"Puerto del Alba\" - \"Port of\n"
"Dawn.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我听到他们叫它“Puerto del Alba”——“黎明\n"
"港”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3051..3845
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/2
msgid ""
"They have perfect visibility of the area from up\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"从上面，他们能看清\n"
"这一带。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3928..4709
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/3
msgid ""
"We did our best to sneak in undetected, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们尽力潜入不被发现，可……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 4959..5544
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/4
msgid ""
"one of the guards spotted us, and we...\n"
msgstr ""
"一个守卫发现了我们，我们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5572..5823
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/5
msgid ""
"What is it?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5837..6840
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/6
msgid ""
"...I'm sorry, you'll have to ask Professor Gálvez the\n"
"rest.\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉，剩下的你得去问 Gálvez\n"
"教授。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 6868..7718
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/7
msgid ""
"...It's OK. You've been through a lot.\n"
msgstr ""
"……没事。你受苦了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 7732..8735
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/8
msgid ""
"I am sorry, I... I just cannot...\n"
msgstr ""
"对不起，我……我说不下去……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 8749..10031
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/9
msgid ""
"You did great, Paz. I won't let your efforts go\n"
"wasted.\n"
msgstr ""
"你做得很好，Paz。我不会让你\n"
"白费。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/0
msgid ""
"This is a tropical rainforest, just like Bosque del\n"
"Alba.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是热带雨林，就像阿尔巴森林\n"
"一样。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/1
msgid ""
"The temperature and humidity can be brutal. El\n"
"Cenegal means \"Place of Mud.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"温湿度可能很严酷。埃尔\n"
"塞内加尔意为“泥泞之地”。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/2
msgid ""
"Mud. Great. I'll watch my step.\n"
msgstr ""
"泥巴。好极了。我会小心的。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/3
msgid ""
"This area often gets flooded by the river.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带常被河水淹没。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/4
msgid ""
"There are canals here and there carved out by the\n"
"water.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里有水流冲刷出来的\n"
"一条条水道。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/5
msgid ""
"Good places to hide.\n"
msgstr ""
"藏身好地方。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/6
msgid ""
"But they'll also make it harder for you to see. Be\n"
"careful, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们也会让你更难看清周围。小\n"
"心，斯内克。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1212
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/0
msgid ""
"There should be a suspension bridge around there.\n"
msgstr ""
"那附近应该有座吊桥。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1713
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/1
msgid ""
"In lowlands like this?\n"
msgstr ""
"这种低地会有？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2633
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/2
msgid ""
"The ground nearby is harder and higher than usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"附近地面比一般更硬更高。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2716..3594
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/3
msgid ""
"The river cut through it, eventually creating a\n"
"valley.\n"
msgstr ""
"河流穿凿而过，最终形成了一道\n"
"山谷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3636..4597
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/4
msgid ""
"There might be another way to get across the\n"
"river somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许还有别的办法可以渡过\n"
"这条河。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5349
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/5
msgid ""
"I wouldn't want to run into someone on the bridge.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可不想在桥上撞见人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5391..6687
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/6
msgid ""
"The valley tends to be misty, so you might not be\n"
"able to see the water from up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"山谷里常常雾气弥漫，所以你在上面可能看\n"
"不到水面。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6770..7314
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/7
msgid ""
"Fall and it'll leave more than a bump.\n"
msgstr ""
"掉下去可不只是摔个包。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/0
msgid ""
"When a river floods an area, the banks can\n"
"collapse, creating a marsh.\n"
msgstr ""
"河流淹没一片区域时，河岸可能\n"
"坍塌，形成沼泽。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/1
msgid ""
"You see a lot of them around here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这附近很多。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/2
msgid ""
"I'll need to watch the noise my feet make in el\n"
"cenegal.\n"
msgstr ""
"我得留意自己在埃尔\n"
"塞内加尔里脚下发出的声响。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/3
msgid ""
"There's a marsh on the other side of the river, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"河对岸也有片沼泽。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/4
msgid ""
"The suspension bridge will take you there.\n"
msgstr ""
"吊桥能通到那边。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 445..1630
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/0
msgid ""
"The river running through here is Río del Jade, or\n"
"\"the Jade River.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"流经这里的是里奥德尔哈德河，即\n"
"“翡翠河”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2438
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/1
msgid ""
"Jade? Are there minerals around here?\n"
msgstr ""
"翡翠？这附近有矿？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3287
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/2
msgid ""
"No, it refers to the color of the water.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，是指水色。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3357..4040
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/3
msgid ""
"You'll have to go to Guatemala for jade.\n"
msgstr ""
"翡翠得去危地马拉才有。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 4096..5475
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/4
msgid ""
"Hmm... Doesn't look all that pretty from where I'm\n"
"standing.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……从我站的地方看，可没那么\n"
"漂亮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 5517..6673
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/5
msgid ""
"We're still in the rainy season, so the river's a little\n"
"muddy.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在还是雨季，所以河水有点\n"
"浑浊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7606
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/6
msgid ""
"It'll return to normal once the dry season starts.\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季一到就会恢复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8554
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/7
msgid ""
"Rivers are an important means of transport around\n"
"here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带的河流是重要的\n"
"运输手段。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 8609..9822
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/8
msgid ""
"They're relatively calm, and there are plenty of\n"
"canals along the coast, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们相对平静，而且沿岸还有\n"
"很多运河。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9863..10978
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/9
msgid ""
"A boat'd be more than enough to transport some\n"
"good-sized cargo.\n"
msgstr ""
"用一艘船来运输一些\n"
"大件货物绰绰有余。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11619
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/10
msgid ""
"Like... a nuclear weapon?\n"
msgstr ""
"比如……核武器？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12887
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/11
msgid ""
"We don't know enough yet. I'll keep looking.\n"
msgstr ""
"目前情报还不够。我继续查。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 12914..13221
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/12
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/29
msgid ""
"Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢你，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/0
msgid ""
"There's a lot of banana cultivation along Costa\n"
"Rica's Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的加勒比海岸沿线\n"
"种植着大量香蕉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2702
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/1
msgid ""
"The area's dotted with banana plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带遍布香蕉种植园。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 2772..3524
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/2
msgid ""
"Bananas have been Costa Rica's main crop\n"
msgstr ""
"香蕉是哥斯达黎加主要作物，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4611
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/3
msgid ""
"since they were introduced from Panama in the\n"
"19th century.\n"
msgstr ""
"自从19世纪它们从巴拿马\n"
"传入以来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4695..5447
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/4
msgid ""
"They bring in a fair amount of foreign currency.\n"
msgstr ""
"带来了相当可观的外汇收入。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5503..6227
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/5
msgid ""
"A real fruta de oro, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是黄金果实啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7453
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/6
msgid ""
"Si. But exporting all those bananas requires a ton\n"
"of land.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。但出口所有这些香蕉需要\n"
"大片土地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 7537..8219
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/7
msgid ""
"Hence all the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以才有了这么多种植园。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 8261..9543
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/8
msgid ""
"Clearing all that forest just to grow bananas robs\n"
"animals of their habitats.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了种香蕉而砍伐所有那些森林，剥夺了\n"
"动物的栖息地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10546
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/9
msgid ""
"I do not know how good that is for Costa Rica in\n"
"the end.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知这最终对哥斯达黎加\n"
"有多大好处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1267
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/0
msgid ""
"Panama disease was rampant here about 20 years\n"
"ago,\n"
msgstr ""
"约20年前，巴拿马病在这里\n"
"肆虐，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1393..2284
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/1
msgid ""
"putting a lot of banana plantations out of business.\n"
msgstr ""
"让许多香蕉种植园倒闭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2354..2716
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/2
msgid ""
"Panama disease?\n"
msgstr ""
"巴拿马病？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2786..3413
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/3
msgid ""
"It is caused by a type of fungus.\n"
msgstr ""
"由一种真菌引起。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 3524..4695
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/4
msgid ""
"Apparently it killed off almost all the banana\n"
"species that used to grow here.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说它几乎杀死了这里曾经生长的\n"
"所有香蕉品种。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4736..5154
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/5
msgid ""
"How could that happen?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么会这样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5224..5893
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/6
msgid ""
"Cultivated bananas do not produce seeds.\n"
msgstr ""
"栽培香蕉不结种子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5948..7481
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/7
msgid ""
"You have to remove and transplant part of the\n"
"stem yourself. You plant them in the fields.\n"
msgstr ""
"你得亲手切下茎的一部分来移植，\n"
"再种到田里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7523..8233
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/8
msgid ""
"So you've got acres of identical plants?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你有大片相同作物？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8275..9487
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/9
msgid ""
"Si. When one plant is infected, the disease spreads\n"
"quickly.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。一株染病，\n"
"就会迅速蔓延。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9599..10407
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/10
msgid ""
"Species lacking genetic diversity become weak.\n"
msgstr ""
"缺基因多样性的物种会变弱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10504..11075
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/11
msgid ""
"They grow different bananas today,\n"
msgstr ""
"如今他们种另一种香蕉，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 11103..11981
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/12
msgid ""
"ones said to be resistant to Panama disease.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说能抵抗巴拿马病。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has several active volcanoes, Irazú\n"
"being one of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加有几座活火山，\n"
"伊拉苏是其中之一。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/1
msgid ""
"That's where \"Camino de Lava\" comes from, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以才有\"熔岩之路\"这名字？\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/2
msgid ""
"The tropical dry forests around here are quite\n"
"different from our rainforests.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带的热带干林\n"
"和我们的雨林大不相同。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/3
msgid ""
"They lose their leaves in the dry season.\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季时它们会落叶。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/4
msgid ""
"Tropical forests are not all thick jungles. A few of\n"
"them even have cacti.\n"
msgstr ""
"热带森林并非都是密林，\n"
"有些甚至长着仙人掌。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/5
msgid ""
"Some of Costa Rica's greatest assets are its\n"
"diverse forests and natural landscapes.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加最宝贵的财富之一，\n"
"就是多样的森林与自然景观。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 445..1588
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/0
msgid ""
"Aldea de los Despiertos means \"Village of the\n"
"Awake.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Aldea de los Despiertos意为\n"
"\"清醒者之村\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 1936..2229
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/1
msgid ""
"Weird name.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字真怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 2270..3510
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/2
msgid ""
"The area's littered with coffee fields and there's a\n"
"factory nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带遍地咖啡田，\n"
"附近还有座工厂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 3608..4569
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/3
msgid ""
"The villagers are fans of coffee, so...\n"
msgstr ""
"村民都是咖啡迷，所以……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/4
msgid ""
"They don't get much sleep, huh? They've got a\n"
"sense of humor all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"难怪他们睡不好，\n"
"还挺有幽默感。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7397
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/5
msgid ""
"I cannot believe they would take over a place like\n"
"this and use it as a prison.\n"
msgstr ""
"真不敢相信他们竟占领这种地方\n"
"当监狱用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8763
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/6
msgid ""
"It is unforgiveable. For both la CIA and the thugs\n"
"they employ.\n"
msgstr ""
"不可原谅。CIA和他们雇的\n"
"暴徒都一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/7
msgid ""
"All the villagers wanted was to live in peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"村民们只想平静地生活。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10490
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/8
msgid ""
"What gives la CIA the right to crush them like\n"
"that?!\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA凭什么这样\n"
"践踏他们？！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11438
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/9
msgid ""
"They don't care about anyone's rights but their\n"
"own.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们只顾自己权利，\n"
"不管别人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/10
msgid ""
"It's just the way some people are.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些人就是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12260..12705
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/11
msgid ""
"You really think so?\n"
msgstr ""
"你真这么想？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12747..14015
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/12
msgid ""
"Don't worry. It just gives me the right to teach\n"
"them a lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"别担心。这正好让我有理由\n"
"教训他们一顿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..2159
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/0
msgid ""
"La CIA has taken control of this coffee factory,\n"
"too. All to produce its drugs...\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA也控制了这家咖啡厂。\n"
"全是为了制毒……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/1
msgid ""
"It was famous once, for its fine beans.\n"
msgstr ""
"它曾以优质咖啡豆闻名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 3482..4722
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/2
msgid ""
"Cafetal Aroma Encantado... \"Enchanting Aroma,\"\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"Cafetal Aroma Encantado……“迷人香气”，\n"
"是吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5823
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/3
msgid ""
"Si. Once we've thrown the mercenaries out of\n"
"Costa Rica,\n"
msgstr ""
"Si。等我们把雇佣兵赶出\n"
"哥斯达黎加，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 5935..6701
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/4
msgid ""
"I know it will make wonderful coffee again.\n"
msgstr ""
"我相信它能再产出好咖啡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7370
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/5
msgid ""
"And then you must come and try some, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"到时候你一定要来尝尝，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 7370..9306
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/6
msgid ""
"Sounds great. I wouldn't mind a cuppa joe after all\n"
"this is over. Oh, wait...\n"
msgstr ""
"听着不错。等这一切结束，我倒不介意\n"
"来杯咖啡。哦，等等……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9334..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/7
msgid ""
"What is wrong?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9599..11215
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/8
msgid ""
"No, I... just remembered this guy I knew who wasn't\n"
"big on coffee. English.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我……刚想起一个认识的人，他不太\n"
"爱喝咖啡。英国人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 11354..12552
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/9
msgid ""
"\"Get rid of that muddy water and get a cup of\n"
"black tea down your gob,\" he'd say.\n"
msgstr ""
"“别喝那泥水了，来杯红茶\n"
"灌进你嘴里，”他总这么说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 12552..13918
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/10
msgid ""
"Ha! That's too bad for him - it is delicious.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈！他亏了，这咖啡好喝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/0
msgid ""
"As I said before, building railroads in Costa Rica\n"
"was a dangerous job.\n"
msgstr ""
"我说过，在哥斯达黎加修铁路\n"
"是危险的工作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2883
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/1
msgid ""
"A lot of men died, and sometimes they stopped\n"
"work altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"很多人死了，有时工程\n"
"干脆停工。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4193
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/2
msgid ""
"This is one of those places. They had to cut\n"
"through steep terrain,\n"
msgstr ""
"这里就是其中之一。他们得穿过\n"
"陡峭地形，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4207..5405
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/3
msgid ""
"so when they finally made it through they just built\n"
"the rail terminal right there.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以好不容易打通后，就直接把\n"
"铁路终点站建在了那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5447..5921
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/4
msgid ""
"And that's why they named it...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以他们叫它……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 46138..64136
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/5
msgid ""
"El Cadalso... the Gallows. Charming.\n"
msgstr ""
"El Cadalso……绞刑台。真迷人。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/6
msgid ""
"I'm surprised the construction money didn't dry up\n"
"the way things were going.\n"
msgstr ""
"照这情形，我很惊讶建设资金\n"
"没枯竭。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/7
msgid ""
"Actually, it did. But the bananas helped complete it,\n"
"so they say.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实确实枯竭了。但据说香蕉\n"
"帮忙建完了它。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/8
msgid ""
"You mean... the energy the workers got from\n"
"eating bananas?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说……工人们吃香蕉\n"
"获得的能量？\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/9
msgid ""
"I suppose they do have plenty of vitamins and...\n"
msgstr ""
"我想香蕉确实富含维生素和……\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/10
msgid ""
"No, no, no, I meant the money they got to finish it\n"
"came from exporting bananas.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不，不，我是说完工的钱\n"
"来自香蕉出口。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/11
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/5
msgid ""
"Oh...\n"
msgstr ""
"哦……\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/12
msgid ""
"But one thing is for certain!\n"
msgstr ""
"但有一点可以肯定！\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/13
msgid ""
"The owners of the railroads expanded into the\n"
"banana trade\n"
msgstr ""
"铁路老板们扩张进了\n"
"香蕉贸易\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/14
msgid ""
"after construction was completed.\n"
msgstr ""
"建设完工之后。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/15
msgid ""
"That was the start of banana cultivation in Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是哥斯达黎加香蕉种植的\n"
"开端。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 459..1741
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/0
msgid ""
"Snake, to the north of the village is a bridge that\n"
"crosses a hydraulic pipe,\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，村子北边有座桥横跨\n"
"一条输水管，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 1783..2549
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/1
msgid ""
"though normally the bridge is not used by people.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过平时没人走那座桥。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2577..3942
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/2
msgid ""
"If you slip you'll fall straight to the bottom of the\n"
"valley. Be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"一滑就会直接摔到谷底。\n"
"小心点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4500
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/3
msgid ""
"What's a channel doing here?\n"
msgstr ""
"这里怎么会有水渠？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5642
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/4
msgid ""
"It is not for irrigation - they're hydroelectric pipes.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是灌溉用的——是水力发电管。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..6534
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/5
msgid ""
"I wonder if they run into Irazú's crater lake.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知是否通到伊拉苏火山口湖。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7509
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/6
msgid ""
"Normally they would build a reservoir at the\n"
"bottom of the valley,\n"
msgstr ""
"通常他们会在山谷底部\n"
"修建一座水库，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8247
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/7
msgid ""
"but it was probably too dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"但大概太危险了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9292
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/8
msgid ""
"Los Cantos means \"Sword Peak.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"洛斯坎托斯意思是“剑峰”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/0
msgid ""
"You should be able to see across the Irazú\n"
"mountain range from there.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里应该能望见整个伊拉苏\n"
"山脉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 1532..3078
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/1
msgid ""
"There are not as many big trees at that elevation,\n"
"and you'll probably be well above the mist.\n"
msgstr ""
"那个海拔大树不多，\n"
"而且你多半在雾层之上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4193
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/2
msgid ""
"It'll be tough to hide up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那上面很难藏身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5099
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/3
msgid ""
"You're not thinking about the scenery right now,\n"
"are you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你现在想的不是风景，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5154..5893
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/4
msgid ""
"Not while I'm surrounded by bad guys.\n"
msgstr ""
"被敌人围着的时候不会。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6617
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/5
msgid ""
"You should have seen it when the country was at\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"你真该看看这个国家和平时的\n"
"样子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 6729..7258
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/6
msgid ""
"I know you'd have been impressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道你一定会喜欢。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8874
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/7
msgid ""
"Well, that'll be our reward for a successful mission.\n"
"Sound good?\n"
msgstr ""
"那就当任务成功的奖励吧。\n"
"行吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 8902..9668
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/8
msgid ""
"Wonderful. Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"太好了，谢谢SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/0
msgid ""
"...There is... an old fort around there.\n"
msgstr ""
"……那附近……有座旧堡垒。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2201
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/1
msgid ""
"What is it, Paz? You sound... upset.\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了，帕兹？你听起来……不太对劲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3705
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/2
msgid ""
"Well... You see, it was built during the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……那是内战时期建的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3733..5015
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/3
msgid ""
"Let me guess: disputes between Costa Rica's\n"
"political parties\n"
msgstr ""
"让我猜猜：哥斯达黎加各政党间的\n"
"争端\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5015..5656
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/4
msgid ""
"escalated into all-out conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"升级成了全面冲突。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6812
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/5
msgid ""
"Sí. Conflict that cost my grandparents their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。那场冲突夺走了我祖父母的命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6924..8303
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/6
msgid ""
"The most senseless sort of war - countrymen\n"
"mindlessly slaughtering their own.\n"
msgstr ""
"最无意义的战争——同胞\n"
"盲目地自相残杀。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9181
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/7
msgid ""
"That fort is a reminder of that senselessness.\n"
msgstr ""
"那座堡垒就是那场无谓战争的见证。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10518
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/8
msgid ""
"Sadly ironic, given who's occupying it now.\n"
msgstr ""
"讽刺的是，如今占领它的正是那些人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11479
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/9
msgid ""
"That war was the reason Costa Rica abolished the\n"
"army.\n"
msgstr ""
"那场战争让哥斯达黎加废除了\n"
"军队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11549..12371
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/10
msgid ""
"Please, Snake! Get them out of our country!\n"
msgstr ""
"求你了，SNAKE！把他们赶出我们的国家！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12385..12928
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/11
msgid ""
"I intend to.\n"
msgstr ""
"我正有此意。\n"

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/0
msgid ""
"Paz, what was the government thinking building a\n"
"power plant at the top of a mountain?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/1
msgid ""
"With no river to replenish the water, the lake would\n"
"dry up pretty quick...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/2
msgid ""
"...If it were an ordinary power plant. But the plan\n"
"called for a pumped storage power plant.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/3
msgid ""
"Pumped storage power plant? Kaz mentioned that,\n"
"too. What is that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/4
msgid ""
"It's a facility that generates electricity by pumping\n"
"water up to the lake,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/5
msgid ""
"then letting it run back down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/6
msgid ""
"Seems Sisyphean to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/7
msgid ""
"If they turned the water into electricity as soon as\n"
"they'd pumped it up, sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/8
msgid ""
"But a pumped storage plant acts as a kind of\n"
"battery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/9
msgid ""
"A battery?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/10
msgid ""
"For instance, they could pump at night,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/11
msgid ""
"when there's surplus electricity, and store it for\n"
"later use.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/12
msgid ""
"If they need extra power during the day,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/13
msgid ""
"they can generate it using water pumped up during\n"
"the night.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/189/0xbdbd0/14
msgid ""
"I get it. It's a little more difficult to adjust output\n"
"with thermal or nuclear plants.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..2410
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/0
msgid ""
"This area is a tropical cloud forest, continually\n"
"covered in a thick mist.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一地区是热带云雾林，常年\n"
"笼罩在浓密的雾气中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 2465..3162
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/1
msgid ""
"It is quite a mystical place.\n"
msgstr ""
"是个很神秘的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 3204..4987
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/2
msgid ""
"Selba de la Leche... \"Forest of Milk.\" I can barely\n"
"see in front of me.\n"
msgstr ""
"牛奶森林……“牛奶之林”。我几乎\n"
"看不清眼前。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6269
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/3
msgid ""
"There you go again. The forest is basically sitting\n"
"in a cloud,\n"
msgstr ""
"你又来了。这片森林基本上就是坐落在\n"
"云里，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7021
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/4
msgid ""
"so of course it's going to be hard to see.\n"
msgstr ""
"看不清是当然的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 7049..8623
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/5
msgid ""
"But you know, the cloud forest is the only place\n"
"many exotic creatures can live.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你知道，云雾林是许多奇异生物\n"
"唯一能生存的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 8637..9849
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/6
msgid ""
"Well, if they're not edible, I'm not interested.\n"
msgstr ""
"不能吃的话我没兴趣。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 9905..10964
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/7
msgid ""
"Snake! I'll have you know people travel from all\n"
"around the world\n"
msgstr ""
"蛇！我告诉你，人们从世界\n"
"各地赶来\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 10964..11772
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/8
msgid ""
"to witness Costa Rica's unique fauna!\n"
msgstr ""
"只为一睹哥斯达黎加独特的动物！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 445..1170
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/0
msgid ""
"Snake, watch out for the frogs.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，小心那些青蛙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2883
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/1
msgid ""
"Why, they bite? Relax, no frog's ever eaten a snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么，会咬人？放心，青蛙吃不了蛇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 3009..4179
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/2
msgid ""
"Although I've feasted on a few frogs' legs myself...\n"
msgstr ""
"不过我自己倒是吃过几只蛙腿……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 4193..5029
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/3
msgid ""
"But, they're dangerous! They're poisonous!\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们很危险！有毒！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5071..5335
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/4
msgid ""
"Poisonous?\n"
msgstr ""
"有毒？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6311
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/5
msgid ""
"Poison dart frogs live up to their name, I assure\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"箭毒蛙名副其实，我向你\n"
"保证。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 6380..7829
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/6
msgid ""
"Their poison is so strong the indígena use them to\n"
"make poison-tipped arrows.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们的毒性如此之强，原住民会用它们\n"
"制作毒箭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 7857..9292
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/7
msgid ""
"Some secrete poison through their skin - even\n"
"touching them can be dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些通过皮肤分泌毒液——甚至\n"
"触碰它们都很危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9961
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/8
msgid ""
"So don't go petting them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别去摸它们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10212..10978
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/9
msgid ""
"So... I can't eat one?\n"
msgstr ""
"我不能吃一个？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11424
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/10
msgid ""
"I'm warning you!\n"
msgstr ""
"我警告你！\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/0
msgid ""
"Catarata de la Muerte means \"Waterfall of Death.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Catarata de la Muerte意为“死亡瀑布”。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/1
msgid ""
"How cheerful.\n"
msgstr ""
"真高兴。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/2
msgid ""
"I am sure it will be no problem for you, Snake,\n"
msgstr ""
"我相信这对你不在话下，SNAKE，\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/3
msgid ""
"especially compared to all the dire situations\n"
"you've faced in the past.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是与你过去所面对的\n"
"那些可怕处境相比。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/4
msgid ""
"Easy to say now. We'll see what really happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在说得轻巧。到时候看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/5
msgid ""
"Sorry. Still, you have surprised me. Everything they\n"
"say about the legend is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。不过你让我吃惊了。关于传说的\n"
"一切果然都是真的。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/6
msgid ""
"I'm neither hero nor legend. But for some reason, I\n"
"don't mind you calling me that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我既非英雄也非传说。但不知为何，\n"
"我不介意你这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/7
msgid ""
"Thanks. Be careful, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。小心点，SNAKE。和平！\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/0
msgid ""
"Selba de la Muerte, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/1
msgid ""
"\"Forest of Death.\" Wouldn't want to get lost here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/2
msgid ""
"Sure wouldn't. But do not worry, I will be your guide.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/3
msgid ""
"Happy to hear it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/4
msgid ""
"By the way, Snake, you know much about sloths?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/5
msgid ""
"Just the name.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/6
msgid ""
"They are amazing. Sloths spend almost all their\n"
"lives up in trees,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/7
msgid ""
"except for when they have to go to the bathroom.\n"
"Plus, they barely eat a thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbecf0/8
msgid ""
"What? How do they survive?\n"
msgstr ""
